rd":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"","name":"Island","oracle_id":"b2c6aa39-2d2a-459c-a555-fb48ba993373","oracle_text":"({T}: Add {U}.)","power":null,"produced_mana":["U"],"released_at":"2026-06-26","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land \u2014 Island"},{"cmc":1.0,"color_identity":["U"],"colors":["U"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"legal","standard":"legal","standardbrawl":"legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{U}","name":"Unsummon","oracle_id":"837182db-1bf3-4a2c-bd01-1af9d9873561","oracle_text":"Return target creature to its owner's hand.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2026-04-24","toughness":null,"type_line":"Instant"},{"cmc":5.0,"color_identity":["B"],"colors":["B"],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"legal","historic":"legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}{B}","name":"Yargle, Glutton of Urborg","oracle_id":"ed66cd31-958f-4b28-82a3-e04acc819afc","oracle_text":"","power":"9","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2023-08-04","toughness":"3","type_line":"Legendary Creature \u2014 Frog Spirit"}],"rulings":[{"comment":"Amass Zombies works the same way, except you create a 0/0 black Zombie Army creature token if you don't control an Army. If the Army creature you chose isn't already a Zombie, it becomes a Zombie in addition to its other types. By combining cards with amass Orcs and amass Zombies, you can end up with an Orc Zombie Army.","oracle_id":"8f98806e-c6b7-44af-b436-88acf36d25ec","published_at":"2023-06-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Amass abilities are now written as \"amass [subtype] N.\" Previous cards with amass have received errata to say \"amass Zombies N.\"","oracle_id":"8f98806e-c6b7-44af-b436-88acf36d25ec","published_at":"2023-06-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gr\u00edma Wormtongue's activated ability checks whether the sacrificed creature was legendary as it last existed on the battlefield. It doesn't matter whether or not it's legendary in the graveyard.","oracle_id":"8f98806e-c6b7-44af-b436-88acf36d25ec","published_at":"2023-06-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an effect says to set an opponent's life total to a number that's higher than the opponent's current life total while Gr\u00edma Wormtongue is on the battlefield, the player's life total doesn't change.","oracle_id":"8f98806e-c6b7-44af-b436-88acf36d25ec","published_at":"2023-06-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If you don't control an Army, the Orc Army token you create enters the battlefield as a 0/0 creature before receiving counters. Any abilities that trigger when a creature with a certain power enters the battlefield, such as that of Mentor of the Meek, will see the token enter as a 0/0 creature before it gets +1/+1 counters.","oracle_id":"8f98806e-c6b7-44af-b436-88acf36d25ec","published_at":"2023-06-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In the rare case that you control multiple Army creatures (perhaps because you played a creature with changeling) while you amass Orcs, you choose which of your Army creatures to put the +1/+1 counters on. If that creature isn't an Orc, it becomes an Orc in addition to its other types.","oracle_id":"8f98806e-c6b7-44af-b436-88acf36d25ec","published_at":"2023-06-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Some cards refer to the \"amassed Army.\" That means the Army creature you chose to receive counters, even if no counters were placed on it for some reason.","oracle_id":"8f98806e-c6b7-44af-b436-88acf36d25ec","published_at":"2023-06-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Some spells and abilities that amass Orcs may require targets. If each target chosen is an illegal target as that spell or ability tries to resolve, it won't resolve. You won't amass Orcs.","oracle_id":"8f98806e-c6b7-44af-b436-88acf36d25ec","published_at":"2023-06-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Spells and abilities that cause opponents to gain life still resolve while Gr\u00edma Wormtongue is on the battlefield. No opponent will gain life, but any other effects of that spell or ability will still happen.","oracle_id":"8f98806e-c6b7-44af-b436-88acf36d25ec","published_at":"2023-06-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"To amass Orcs N, if you don't control an Army creature, create a 0/0 black Orc Army creature token. Then you choose an Army creature you control and put N +1/+1 counters on it. If that Army isn't already an Orc, it becomes an Orc in addition to its other types.","oracle_id":"8f98806e-c6b7-44af-b436-88acf36d25ec","published_at":"2023-06-16","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Falkenrath Aristocrat's activated ability checks whether the sacrificed creature was a Human as it last existed on the battlefield. It doesn't matter what its creature types are in the graveyard.","oracle_id":"cd2a87c4-d1c3-4a9e-b2df-e6fe251421c4","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If the sacrificed creature was a Human, Falkenrath Aristocrat gains indestructible and also gets a +1/+1 counter.","oracle_id":"cd2a87c4-d1c3-4a9e-b2df-e6fe251421c4","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can sacrifice Falkenrath Aristocrat to pay the cost of its own ability. It won't receive a counter or gain indestructible, but it will enable abilities that check when or if a creature dies.","oracle_id":"cd2a87c4-d1c3-4a9e-b2df-e6fe251421c4","published_at":"2020-08-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The ability checks whether the sacrificed creature as it last existed on the battlefield was a Human. (It doesn\u2019t matter what its creature types are in the graveyard.)","oracle_id":"f578a5e0-77e2-4c35-90b2-6628ed9b218e","published_at":"2011-01-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"You can sacrifice Falkenrath Torturer itself to activate its ability.","oracle_id":"f578a5e0-77e2-4c35-90b2-6628ed9b218e","published_at":"2011-01-22","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
